  <h1>Single Image Editor: Edit, Compare &amp; Export One Photo in Detail</h1>

  <div class="blog-meta">
    <span class="blog-meta-badge">How-to</span>
    <span>September 30, 2026</span>
    <span>· 7 min read</span>
  </div>

  <p>
    The KodiniTools batch editor is built for many images at once. Sometimes, though, a single photo needs special treatment: a tilted horizon, a subject that is too dark, a title that should go on the image, or a crop for a profile picture. That is what the single image editor is for. It opens one image from your series in its own window, shows every change live with a before/after comparison and exports the result straight to a file. Everything runs in your browser, with no installation and no upload.
  </p>

